  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 152706765a7dec6419e3ec12554375ac, type: 3}
  m_Name: BusinessPortalCourse
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  courseName: Business Portal Course
  courseDescription: Tools and frameworks to validate, build, and launch your business faster.
  accentColor: {r: 0.13, g: 0.55, b: 0.88, a: 1}
  lessons:
  - title: What to Consider for your Biz Model & Niche
    description: Learn what to consider when selecting your business model and niche
      so you can get to market faster and start testing without getting stuck in analysis
      paralysis. This chapter covers passion versus purchasing power, why you should
      niche down first, why boring niches can be reliable, why customer lifetime value
      matters, and why competition is a sign of market demand.
    videoUrl: https://www.loom.com/embed/35fa2e8a707646808db0d81e9bc5e9f1
    thumbnail: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Create Your Business Summary
    description: Create a clear business summary based on whether you already have
      an offer or still need help building one. If you already have an offer, use
      the V2 Biz Summary Generator. If you do not have an offer yet, use the Business
      Model and Offer Generator. The summary will appear below the questions and will
      not be sent to your email.
    videoUrl: https://www.loom.com/embed/90849a72965841eab0986ab046cf6ea8
    thumbnail: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Generate Your Knowledgebase
    description: Use the Knowledgebase AI Agent to turn your business summary into
      a structured knowledgebase. Make sure you are using the most up-to-date version
      of chat before generating it. This step helps organize your business model,
      offer, niche, positioning, and customer information.
    videoUrl: https://www.loom.com/embed/25a0a535208a46d0b7dea9732d2d34d5
    thumbnail: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Output Your DFY Business Blueprint
    description: Build a realistic Done-For-You business blueprint for the opportunity
      you described. The blueprint should include your ideal customer profile, market
      size, core pains, desired outcomes, single DFY offer, customer avatars, pricing
      model, competitor snapshot, MVP launch path, and scale-readiness checklist.
      The goal is to create something practical, monetizable, and ready to execute.
    videoUrl: https://www.loom.com/embed/caf581770e48436d960a8fd3be9c31a7
    thumbnail: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Market Audit
    description: Check whether your market is hungry, proven, and already spending
      money. Make sure you are selling to one clear niche, buyers already search for
      solutions, the pain is urgent or expensive, and competitors are already making
      money. If the market is not starving, no offer can fix it.
    videoUrl: https://www.loom.com/embed/de2ac2ae80a443418c0d31eef8baf155
    thumbnail: {fileID: 0}
